Something happened here... or rather, something didn't.

The light in the sky grew brighter and brighter, until one evening it was as bright as the moon. The dinosaurs looked up. The tiny mammals hid deeper in their burrows.

And then the meteor missed.

It passed so close that it scraped the top of the atmosphere, painted the whole sky orange for a night, and kept going into the dark. By morning it was just a fading dot.

The triceratops went back to grazing. The T. rex went back to its bad mood. The ferns kept growing.

The dinosaurs survived. In this timeline, the age of the dinosaurs never ended.
